    "content": "Dezembro (December) is the 12th and final month of the year in the Gregorian calendar, containing 31 days. It marks the beginning of winter in the Northern Hemisphere and summer in the Southern Hemisphere. The name originates from the Latin word decem (ten), as it was originally the 10th month. Key Information regarding \"Dezembro\": Definition: The last month of the year, following November. Etymology: Derived from Latin December. Birthstones: Turquoise, zircon, and tanzanite. Birth Flower: Narcissus. Cultural Context: In Portugal, 1º Dezembro (December 1st) is a recognized sports club, while Dez de Dezembro (December 10th) refers to a posthumous album by Brazilian singer Cássia Eller. Common Uses: It is used in Portuguese context for end-of-year celebrations (festas de dezembro). The term is often used in administrative or financial contexts, such as project budgeting (o orçamento do projeto estava no osso).",
